 ## Languages

 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
-`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server selects a supported language from the
+request's `Accept-Language` header, using the highest nonzero q-value
+(default 1) and header order to break ties. Region tags such as `ko-KR`
+and `en-US` select their base language. Unsupported or malformed entries
+are ignored; if no supported language is acceptable, the server uses
+`LARDER_LANG` (default `en`). All error codes, including `internal` (500),
+have messages in both languages.
